    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7494" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cĕrăsus</span></b> , i,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρασος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the cherrytree</i>,
			brought by Lucullus from Cerasus, in Pontus, to Italy, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 39, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. G.
				2, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 15, 25, 30, § 102</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Col.
				11, 2, 96</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. Nuc. 32
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A cherry</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 4</span></i> (5), 2, 15; in prose,
			instead of it, <i>neutr.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cĕrăsum</span></b> ,
			i, <i><span class="en">Cels. 2, 24, 27</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Pall. Oct. 12, 7
			al.</span></i>—Of doubtful gender: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ceraso,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					6, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cerasorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 25, 30, § 102</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">15, 28, 34,
				§ 112</span></i>.</div>
